    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2019-june/q1",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 &amp; -5 \\\\ 2 &amp; -7 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Show that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{M}\"></span> is non-singular.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> of the plane is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{M}\"></span>.</p><p>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is transformed to the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> by the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> is 63 square units,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) find the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Show that the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 2x\"></span> is invariant under the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
