      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2019-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^3 + 6x^2 - 3x + 12 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha, \\beta\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span>.</p><p>Without solving the equation, find the cubic equation whose roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\alpha + 3), (\\beta + 3)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\gamma + 3)\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"pw^3 + qw^2 + rw + s = 0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p, q, r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
