      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2019-june/q5",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:82mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2019-june/q05-figure-1.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Complex numbers plotted on an Argand diagram.\"></figure><p>The complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1 = -2\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2 = -1 + 2i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3 = 1 + i\"></span> are plotted in Figure 1, on an Argand diagram for the complex plane with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z = x + iy\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Explain why <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span> cannot all be roots of a quartic polynomial equation with real coefficients.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arg\\left(\\frac{z_2 - z_1}{z_3 - z_1}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arctan(2) - \\arctan\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>A copy of Figure 1, labelled Diagram 1, is given on page 12.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Shade, on Diagram 1, the set of points of the complex plane that satisfy the inequality</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z + 2| \\leq |z - 1 - i|\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:82mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2019-june/q05-figure-2.svg\" alt=\"Diagram 1. Argand diagram for shading in part (d).\"></figure>",
