      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = 2x^{\\frac{1}{3}} + x^{-\\frac{2}{3}} \\quad x &gt; 0\"></span></p><p>The finite region bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span>, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = \\frac{1}{8}\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 8\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> radians about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis to form a solid of revolution.</p><p>Given that the volume of the solid formed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{461}{2}\"></span> units cubed, use algebraic integration to find the angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> through which the region is rotated.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></p>",
